{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Step 9:} Copy your data into your spreadsheet and create a copy of your responses. You want to save an original version of your data along with the coded data. You can create a copy by right-clicking on the spreadsheet tab, selecting \u8220"Move or Copy,\u8221" and selecting to copy. This will create a new tab with the same data \u8211- name these tabs \u8220"Original Responses\u8221" and \u8220"Coded Responses\u8221" to ensure these don\u8217't get mixed up.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Step 10:} Once you have a copy of your responses to edit, you should start coding all of the responses based on your codebook. Coding will look different depending on your types of variables. Ask your UCA any questions about specific variables.\par}
